[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3235688035","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110073#issuecomment-3235688035","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110073","id":3235688035,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7A3K5j","user":{"login":"Lielay9","id":40064911,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwMDY0OTEx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/40064911?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lielay9","html_url":"https://github.com/Lielay9","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lielay9/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lielay9/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lielay9/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lielay9/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lielay9/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lielay9/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lielay9/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lielay9/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lielay9/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-29T04:34:09Z","updated_at":"2025-08-29T04:40:15Z","body":"Hmm I don't think this is quite it.\r\n\r\n<img width=\"573\" height=\"285\" alt=\"broken-line\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f9d732c1-0b22-41d9-8729-8c07ab9c94c0\" />\r\n\r\nThe line where the center is added should be removed altogether - the first vertex doesn't have to be added as it already is present in the vertex array. Then below, where triangles are constructed with indices, one index of every triangle should point to the first vertex (the one that originally pointed to the center). Also, the function should not create the first and last vertices in the arc and instead share the corner vertices from where the line starts to avoid issues similar to https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100020 (might even be necessary to fix #110030 properly). That would also need to be fixed for the joints.\r\n\r\nEdit: That's a probably bit more involved fix than what you singed in for - sorry for making it sound so simple in the issue. You can obviously continue if you have the time to spare but also do not feel pressured to do so.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3235688035/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3237570638","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110073#issuecomment-3237570638","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110073","id":3237570638,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7A-WhO","user":{"login":"jz009","id":56200900,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2MjAwOTAw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/56200900?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jz009","html_url":"https://github.com/jz009","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jz009/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jz009/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jz009/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jz009/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jz009/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jz009/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jz009/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jz009/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jz009/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-29T16:18:34Z","updated_at":"2025-08-29T16:18:34Z","body":"There is already a function for creating arcs based on preexisting vertices in the file, used for round joints. I think we can repurpose it here. It's just a bit harder for the begin cap because it is drawn before any vertices of the line exist, but we can call `strip_begin` first in this case and not call it later. I tested more thoroughly this time and I didn't see any difference in behavior from main (minus the gaps not longer being present) but please let me know if you find anything wrong. ","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3237570638/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]